{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1224324-blurry-rules-concerning-casting-effects-and-spending-quintessence-points","id":1224324,"title":"Blurry rules concerning casting Effects and spending Quintessence points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-03T05:29:13-07:00","id":1224324,"title":"Blurry rules concerning casting Effects and spending Quintessence points","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I come to you with a few questions concerning blurry rules to apply when you perform Magick.<br /> <br /> 1 - <u>Mixed effects</u> :<br /> Say you want to perform a mixed Forces/Entropy Effect to enchance the damage of a bullet and to hit the weak spots. Say you hit on your Dex+Firearms roll and get two successes on the Arete roll. With the Forces Sphere used, it means you have 3 successes to calculate the damage, and thus do 6 levels of lethal damage. When does the Entropy part of the spell come into action ? Do you split the successes in some way to make the Entropy part of the spell do something ? The rule book is not quite clear about that (M20 p.415 for instance).<br /> Another example, you need to chanel quintessence when performing a complex ritual. You add Prime 3 to the mix. Do you split the successes to say how much point per round you can get from the Prime part of the spell ? Or, during a ritual, do you make the player roll two rituals (one with the Prime 3 effect to know how much quintessence he can use and for how long) then the ritual itself that will use the quintessence ?<br /> <br /> 2 - <u>Spending quintessence</u> :<br /> I have trouble knowing when I need to spend quintessence points in an Effect and when it is not necessary. I must miss something because there are contradictory rules in the M20 corebook and in HDYDT. Example : Conjunring new Patterns. The Fireball : You need Forces 3 / Prime 2. Do you need to spend Quintessence points ? Sources :<br /> M20 corebook p.537 : Other uses for quintessence in magick : Fueling new patterns so that Life, Forces and Matter can be created from scratch.<br /> HDYDT p.18 : The Basics : To conjure basic material from \u201cnowhere,\u201d combine the appropriate Sphere with Prime 2. Creating a rock, for instance, would take Matter 3/ Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your answers ! I'm trying to answer some newbies' questions and they got me stuck on several points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T07:41:44-07:00","id":1224360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1224324-blurry-rules-concerning-casting-effects-and-spending-quintessence-points#post1224324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> <br /> I come to you with a few questions concerning blurry rules to apply when you perform Magick.<br /> <br /> 1 - <u>Mixed effects</u> :<br /> Say you want to perform a mixed Forces/Entropy Effect to enchance the damage of a bullet and to hit the weak spots. Say you hit on your Dex+Firearms roll and get two successes on the Arete roll. With the Forces Sphere used, it means you have 3 successes to calculate the damage, and thus do 6 levels of lethal damage. When does the Entropy part of the spell come into action ? Do you split the successes in some way to make the Entropy part of the spell do something ? The rule book is not quite clear about that (M20 p.415 for instance).<br /> Another example, you need to chanel quintessence when performing a complex ritual. You add Prime 3 to the mix. Do you split the successes to say how much point per round you can get from the Prime part of the spell ? Or, during a ritual, do you make the player roll two rituals (one with the Prime 3 effect to know how much quintessence he can use and for how long) then the ritual itself that will use the quintessence ?<br /> <br /> 2 - <u>Spending quintessence</u> :<br /> I have trouble knowing when I need to spend quintessence points in an Effect and when it is not necessary. I must miss something because there are contradictory rules in the M20 corebook and in HDYDT. Example : Conjunring new Patterns. The Fireball : You need Forces 3 / Prime 2. Do you need to spend Quintessence points ? Sources :<br /> M20 corebook p.537 : Other uses for quintessence in magick : Fueling new patterns so that Life, Forces and Matter can be created from scratch.<br /> HDYDT p.18 : The Basics : To conjure basic material from \u201cnowhere,\u201d combine the appropriate Sphere with Prime 2. Creating a rock, for instance, would take Matter 3/ Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your answers ! I'm trying to answer some newbies' questions and they got me stuck on several points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mixed effects:<br /> <br /> First thing you should be answering is what exactly are you trying to cast. If the effect is &quot;enhance damage and attack weak point&quot; then I'd rule you need to split your successes to target, and damage as usual for the forces part, and then consider the minimum successes needed for the bullet to &quot;happen&quot; to hit the weak point depending on what it is your aiming at. So if you're trying to shoot at guy wearing bullet proof vest, then I'd say 3 successes should be enough to ignore the armour's benefit.<br /> Similarly, it depends what you're trying to do with Prime. Successes used for one part of an effect cannot be used for another simultaneously. Complex stuff simply need more successes to run.<br /> <br /> As a general rule of thumb for mixed effects, consider how it would be ruled if the effects were done separately, and rule it accordingly. The more complicated an effect, the more successes it requires.<br /> <br /> Spending Quintessence:<br /> <br /> This is a more debatable point and it really dose differ from ST to ST, but I always rule in favour of requiring a source of quintessence for any kind of Prime involved conjurings. At Prime 2, that source of quintessence must invariably come from your own supply, and arguably from a nearby node, but at Prime 3 you should be able to summon it from a periapt, Tass, or even from other willing mages. Higher levels of Prime will allow you to rend quintessence straight out of objects, living beings, and even out of the air if done with enough time. Those of course a lot of that will depend on the Mage's individual interpretation of how Prime functions and where Quintessence comes from.<br /> <br /> Also, feel free to disregard any of the contradicting parts of HDYDT. It's better used as a toybox, than a manual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:13:40-07:00","id":1225252,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much. That's more or less what I had in mind. I tend to use the &quot;split the successes&quot; rule a lot. What I sometimes wonder is when is it OK to do that in one round? and when do you need different arete rolls for your effects? Forces / Entropy seems like one single Effect for me, but channeling quintessence, then use it to create a wonder for example, seems different effects. I think it kind of depend on the situation.<br /> <br /> Concerning the quintessence spending question, I have much trouble setting my mind. I would tend to do the same as you, meaning requiring quintessence for conjurations. Though it does seems hard for the players. Quintessence is rare. I think it would be hard on them to make them pay each time. Still need to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 06-06-2018, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:39:16-07:00","id":1225260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1224324-blurry-rules-concerning-casting-effects-and-spending-quintessence-points?p=1225252#post1225252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the quintessence spending question, I have much trouble setting my mind. I would tend to do the same as you, meaning requiring quintessence for conjurations. Though it does seems hard for the players. Quintessence is rare. I think it would be hard on them to make them pay each time. Still need to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think it's inconvenient, don't do it.<br /> <br /> If all you need it's a metaphysical justification, a theory that I like it's that you're shaping the free floating quintessence (that you know exist everywhere but still can't purify in big-Q Quintessence) in the form that you want to manifest. It would be like transforming air into fire (Forces 3/Matter2), just it's not air.<br /> <br /> Or make Quintessence less rare.<br /> <br /> Being lenient with the Prime 3 power to release Quintessence from patterns may be all you need. You could also increase the amount of juice provided by Nodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:39:59-07:00","id":1225261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1224324-blurry-rules-concerning-casting-effects-and-spending-quintessence-points?p=1225252#post1225252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the quintessence spending question, I have much trouble setting my mind. I would tend to do the same as you, meaning requiring quintessence for conjurations. Though it does seems hard for the players. Quintessence is rare. I think it would be hard on them to make them pay each time. Still need to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You as the ST are in control of how rare quintessence is. Prime users can always use Prime 1 to seek out nodes, Tass, and the like if they needed them, so if it\u2019s really a problem then sprinkle a few more into the game. I imagine that 1 dot nodes are pretty commonplace and only really defended by small groups if at all. Some may be so well hidden they aren\u2019t even on most mages radar. Some 2 point nodes might have chantries built around them, and could require an exchange of favours to access.<br /> And wherever there\u2019s a node, there is Tass. Also, it\u2019s a really effective tool to let your players get really comfortable with a node and start using quintessence like it was water, and then make the node start to run dry. They get really invested in trying to save the node or at the least searching for another one, and can lead to new plot motivators, especially if it\u2019s drying up is related to the plot you had in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-07-2018, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}